cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BoundSec: Coverage-Guided Security Fuzzing for LLM Agents"
message: "If you use BoundSec in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ben Bait"
    given-names: "Mohamed Seddik"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-06"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - AI security
  - LLM agents
  - coverage-guided fuzzing
  - prompt injection
  - red-teaming
abstract: >-
  BoundSec reframes LLM-agent red-teaming as greybox fuzzing. It defines
  behavioural coverage - a black-box analogue of edge coverage for stochastic
  tool-calling policies - over five dimensions (action, transition, guardrail,
  fault, novelty), and drives a coverage-guided evolutionary search (power-scheduled
  corpus + discounted-UCB operator bandit). A deterministic Agent Gym with planted
  canaries, ground-truth labels, and independently-toggleable defense layers makes
  detector precision/recall and search bug-recall measurable. Across a naive-to-frontier
  hardening spectrum, coverage-guided search recovers substantially more of the
  reachable vulnerabilities than static payload replay under a fixed query budget.
